            <ArticleTitle>Inhibition of N-type calcium channels by fluorophenoxyanilide derivatives.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2030-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/md13042030</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A set of fluorophenoxyanilides, designed to be simplified analogues of previously reported ω-conotoxin GVIA mimetics, were prepared and tested for N-type calcium channel inhibition in a SH-SY5Y neuroblastoma FLIPR assay. N-type or Cav2.2 channel is a validated target for the treatment of refractory chronic pain. Despite being significantly less complex than the originally designed mimetics, up to a seven-fold improvement in activity was observed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
